{"id":"kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg","corpus":"aws","title":"Kinesis Video Streams","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisvideostreams-webrtc-dg/latest/devguide/what-is-kvswebrtc.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Kinesis Video Streams"},{"kind":"p","text":"WebRTC is an open technology specification for enabling real-time communication (RTC) across browsers and mobile applications via simple APIs. It uses peering techniques for real-time data exchange between connected peers and provides low latency media streaming required for human-to-human interaction. The WebRTC specification includes a set of IETF protocols including Interactive Connectivity Establishment, Traversal Using Relay around NAT (TURN), and Session Traversal Utilities for NAT (STUN) for establishing peer-to-peer connectivity, in addition to protocol specifications for reliable and secure real-time media and data streaming."},{"kind":"p","text":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams provides a standards-compliant WebRTC implementation as a fully managed capability. You can use Amazon Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC to securely live stream media or perform two-way audio or video interaction between any camera IoT device and WebRTC-compliant mobile or web players. As a fully managed capability, you don't have to build, operate, or scale any WebRTC-related cloud infrastructure, such as signaling or media relay servers to securely stream media across applications and devices."},{"kind":"p","text":"Using Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC, you can easily build applications for live peer-to-peer media streaming, or real-time audio or video interactivity between camera IoT devices, web browsers, and mobile devices for a variety of use cases. Such applications can help parents keep an eye on their baby’s room, enable homeowners to use a video doorbell to check who’s at the door, enable owners of camera-enabled robot vacuums to remotely control the robot by viewing the live camera stream on a mobile phone, and so on."},{"kind":"p","text":"If you're a first-time user of Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC, we recommend that you read the following sections:"},{"kind":"li","text":"How it works"},{"kind":"li","text":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC SDK in C for embedded devices"},{"kind":"li","text":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams with WebRTC SDK in JavaScript for web applications"},{"kind":"li","text":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC SDK for Android"},{"kind":"li","text":"Amazon Kinesis Video Streams WebRTC SDK for iOS"},{"kind":"li","text":"Control plane APIs"},{"kind":"li","text":"Data plane REST APIs"},{"kind":"li","text":"Data plane Websocket APIs"}],"lemmas":{"kineses":["kineses","kinesis"],"videos":["video","videos"],"streams":["stream","streams"],"streamed":["streamed","stream"],"opens":["open","opens"],"opened":["opened","open"],"opening":["opening","open"],"technologies":["technology","technologies"],"enabling":["enabling","enable"],"enablings":["enablings","enabling"],"enables":["enables","enable"],"reals":["real","reals"],"times":["time","times"],"timed":["timed","time"],"timing":["timing","time"],"communications":["communication","communications"],"acrosses":["acrosses","across"],"browsers":["browser","browsers"],"mobiles":["mobile","mobiles"],"applications":["application","applications"],"vias":["vias","via"],"simples":["simple","simples"],"apis":["apis","api"],"uses":["use","uses"],"used":["used","use"],"peering":["peering","peer"],"peerings":["peerings","peering"],"peered":["peered","peer"],"techniques":["technique","techniques"],"data":["datum","data"],"exchanges":["exchange","exchanges"],"exchanging":["exchanging","exchange"],"exchanged":["exchanged","exchange"],"connected":["connected","connect"],"connecteds":["connecteds","connected"],"connects":["connects","connect"],"connecting":["connecting","connect"],"peers":["peer","peers"],"provides":["provides","provide"],"provided":["provided"